Falsifies `paging::aarch64::verification::the_leaf_keeps_address_and_permissions_apart`.

The defect: `leaf_entry` no longer sets `TABLE_OR_PAGE`, so every last-level descriptor
the kernel installs has descriptor type `0b01`. At levels 0 to 2 that is a block mapping;
at level 3, which is where leaves live, `0b01` is reserved and the MMU faults on it. Every
user mapping in the system stops translating. The bit is one term in a four-term `or`, and
nothing else in the crate reads it back.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(leaf & 0b11, 0b11)`, on every input.

**Measured blind before milestone 211.** The harness asserted only
`entry_pa(leaf) == pa` and `leaf_flags(leaf) == flags`, and neither accessor reads the
descriptor-type field: `entry_pa` masks the address bits and `leaf_flags` reads AP, UXN,
PXN, nG and the attribute index. So the descriptor could stop being a page descriptor at
all with both round trips intact. Confirmed by applying this diff against the old phrasing
and watching it stay green.

The same rewrite added the address-field assertion, which catches the encoder/decoder pair
moving together; `sv39.verification.the_leaf_keeps_address_and_permissions_apart.patch`
records that half.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/aarch64.rs b/crates/paging/src/aarch64.rs
index b6d7a0a8..e6ba17d1 100644
--- a/crates/paging/src/aarch64.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/aarch64.rs
@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@ impl PageFormat for Aarch64 {
 
     fn leaf_entry(pa: u64, flags: Flags) -> u64 {
         // At L3, `0b11` means PAGE, not TABLE. Same bits, different meaning by level.
-        (pa & ADDR_MASK) | Self::attrs(flags) | TABLE_OR_PAGE | VALID
+        (pa & ADDR_MASK) | Self::attrs(flags) | VALID
     }
 
     fn leaf_flags(entry: u64) -> Flags {
